<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds reversed early losses on Monday to close higher and traders said they expected to see further gains in coming sessions.</p>
<p>&quot;Bonds initially reacted to the losses seen in other markets on Friday, but they soon turned around with the rebound seen elsewhere,&quot; said one dealer. Spanish financial markets were closed on Friday for Constitution Day.</p>
<p>Dealers said the market was now focussing on a possible cut of at least 25 basis points by the Bank of Spain in its key money market rate on Friday.</p>
</text>
